   196	<h2>Firebase safety checklist</h2>
   197	<ul>
   198	  <li>Every new collection (<code>members</code>, <code>memberProfiles</code>, <code>staffRoster</code>) gets an explicit rule and rules tests in the same commit as the code that writes it (E-2).</li>
   199	  <li>The only writer to <code>my-clay-hub</code>'s member data is <code>ingestMemberUpdate</code> (a transaction; partial updates; never deletes; strips undefined/empty).</li>
   200	  <li>Nothing ever writes to <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>: <code>clayhub-link@</code> holds read-only rights; tested in E-6 (a write attempt is refused).</li>
   201	  <li>Emulator tests only; no test reaches either production project; the CLI credential file is never read.</li>
   202	  <li>Bulk effect is bounded: reconcile and recompute stop above 10% status changes / 5% removals.</li>
   203	  <li>Vault gate before real data; the vault export keeps running weekly.</li>
   204	</ul>
   205	
   206	<h2>Completeness check — if it's interrupted</h2>
   207	<ul>
   208	  <li>E-0…E-4 are code on branches: nothing live until merged and deployed.</li>
   209	  <li>E-5 halfway: Console state visible; re-read and continue. Nothing uses the accounts until E-6.</li>
   210	  <li>E-6 deployed but E-7 not: ingest is live with no callers except the probe — harmless.</li>
   211	  <li>E-7 deployed but E-8 not run: triggers send only members whose docs are edited; the projection is partial and nothing reads it (no sign-in until Phase F). The next 6-hourly reconcile fills it anyway.</li>
   212	  <li>Stop the link at once: pause the reconcile job and remove <code>run.invoker</code> on <code>ingestmemberupdate</code> by redeploying with an empty invoker list (guarded); triggers then fail and retry harmlessly.</li>
   213	</ul>
   214	
