/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/firebase-functions-deploy-guard.html:559:  <li><strong>Sep 29, D2-0:</strong> ✅ Christie ran <code>brew install node@22</code>, which also upgraded 12 shared Homebrew libraries. Checked: <code>/opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/bin/node</code> → <code>v22.23.3</code>; its npm → <code>10.9.9</code>. The default <code>node</code> is unchanged: <code>v20.20.2</code> from <strong>nvm</strong> (<code>~/.nvm/versions/node/v20.20.2</code>), not <code>/usr/local</code> as K14 and F5 had assumed. <strong>Pinning detail for F5:</strong> <code>node@22/bin/npm</code> is a symlink to <code>npm-cli.js</code>, whose shebang runs whatever <code>node</code> is on <code>PATH</code> (Node 20). So <code>$NPM22</code> means <code>"$NODE22" /opt/homebrew/opt/node@22/lib/node_modules/npm/bin/npm-cli.js</code>, never the bare <code>npm</code> symlink, and the preflight asserts <code>"$NPM22" --version</code> = <code>10.9.9</code> (or the logged current version). <strong>Next:</strong> D2-1.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/firebase-functions-deploy-guard.html:560:  <li><strong>Sep 29, D2-1 step 1:</strong> Cloud Build → Settings (the "Permissions" page) pre-selects <code>760301318440-compute@developer.gserviceaccount.com</code>, so the <strong>provisional build account is the Compute account</strong>. All 17 role toggles there show "Disabled", so the Compute account holds none of them, including Cloud Build Service Account and Logs Writer. The account dropdown offers <code>firebase-adminsdk-fbsvc@</code>, <code>functions-build@</code>, <strong><code>my-clay-hub@appspot.gserviceaccount.com</code></strong> and the Compute account; the legacy <code>…@cloudbuild</code> account isn't selectable there, as expected. The Service Accounts list (screenshot) shows <strong>both default accounts now exist and are enabled</strong>: "Default compute service account" and "App Engine default service account". Neither existed at D-1 step 10 (Sep 28), so Google most likely created them after D-1 step 9 enabled the APIs. No build or function has ever run. <strong>Consequences:</strong> step 2 (enable the Compute Engine API) is <strong>not needed</strong>. The App Engine default account is a <strong>new candidate for Editor</strong> and is added to step 3: remove Editor from it if present. Next: IAM "View by roles".</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/firebase-functions-deploy-guard.html:561:  <li><strong>Sep 29, D2-1 step 3:</strong> ✅ IAM "View by roles", with Google-provided grants included (screenshot). <strong>No Editor role exists in the project</strong>, so step 3 had nothing to remove; the organization likely blocks automatic default-account grants. The Compute account and <code>my-clay-hub@appspot</code> hold <strong>no</strong> project roles. <strong>Cloud Build Service Account</strong> is held only by <code>760301318440@cloudbuild.gserviceaccount.com</code> ("Legacy Cloud Build Service Account"), which step 4 removes. Owner (1): Christie@tinkerartstudio.com, the source of <code>actAs</code> (M7; this also covers the Owner-confirmation step). The other roles are Google service agents, as at D-1: Cloud Build, Cloud Functions, Cloud Run, Cloud Scheduler, Cloud Storage for Firebase, Container Registry, Firebase Admin SDK Administrator, Firebase Rules System, Firebase Service Management, Firestore, Service Account Token Creator (1) and Storage Admin (1).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/firebase-functions-deploy-guard.html:562:  <li><strong>Sep 29, D2-1 step 4:</strong> ✅ Christie removed <strong>Cloud Build Service Account</strong> (<code>roles/cloudbuild.builds.builder</code>) from <code>760301318440@cloudbuild.gserviceaccount.com</code>. The "View by roles" screenshot afterwards shows the role gone. The list is now: Google service agents, Owner (Christie), Service Account Token Creator (1) and Storage Admin (1). <strong>Neither build candidate holds Editor or Cloud Build Service Account.</strong> Next: O5 (confirm the bucket names), then step 5 (grant O3 to the Compute account).</li>
