/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:183:<tr><td>D2</td><td>Where functions live</td><td><code>studio-hub/functions/</code>, codebase <code>clayhub-link</code> (the link only), plus <code>my-clay-hub/functions/</code> (everything else). Both deploy <strong>only through a functions-aware guard</strong> (agreed Sep 27). <strong>Amended Sep 29 (M1):</strong> each project gets its own, separate functions guard, as each has its own rules guard — <code>my-clay-hub</code>'s in Phase D2, <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>' at the start of Phase E, when the link code exists. Neither can reach the other project.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:187:    <li>finds <strong>exactly one</strong> <code>members</code> doc with that <code>emailLower</code> that is <strong>not tombstoned</strong> and whose derived status allows sign-in (<code>active</code>, <code>paused</code> or <code>review</code>, per D4). Otherwise it refuses and clears any old claim;</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:191:<tr><td>D4</td><td>What decides a member's status</td><td>A single tested function, <code>deriveStatus(source, todayDenver)</code>. It uses Denver calendar dates and parses <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> strings as dates, never through <code>new Date()</code>. It runs <strong>inside <code>ingestMemberUpdate</code></strong> on every write (Phase E), and again for everyone at <strong>3:30 AM Denver</strong> daily (Phase E; this avoids the DST gap). Rules are applied in order; the first match wins:
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:200:    <li>Any valid pause window with <strong>start ≤ today ≤ end</strong> (both days included; D4a) → <code>paused</code></li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:205:<tr><td>D4a</td><td>What does a pause's end date mean?</td><td><strong>The last paused day</strong> (Christie, Sep 27). A pause entered as Jan 2 – Feb 1 means the member is back on Feb 2, and the app says "Booking opens back up on Feb 2". Membership Manager currently gets this wrong by one day (finding 3); Phase B fixes it.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:212:<tr><td>D11</td><td>Permissions inventory (copied into the resilience plan's IAM inventory)</td><td>See <a href="#iam">the IAM inventory</a> below. Every grant runs one way, uses dedicated service accounts, and needs no key files.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:242:<tr><td>D21</td><td>Permanent member ID</td><td>Approved (Christie, Sep 27). Built in Phase B, which is on hold until her other Membership Manager session is merged.
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:248:<tr><td>D22</td><td>How the link delivers changes</td><td>Approved (Christie, Sep 27). <strong>"Re-read, then send a snapshot."</strong>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:264:  Because every message is the whole truth as of its read time, arrival order, retries, deletes and email changes (the new doc and the retired old doc in one batch) all end in the right state. <code>users/{uid}</code> works the same way, into <code>staffRoster/staff_{uid}</code>, using that document read's <code>DocumentSnapshot.readTime</code>. There's no <code>memberId</code> and no conflict case on that path. Docs without a <code>memberId</code> are skipped with an alert (Phase E requires Phase B). <strong>Phone (keeps SPEC DECISIONS #24):</strong> the snapshot carries only <code>phoneLast4</code>, worked out in <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>. The full phone number never leaves that project. No client can read <code>members/*</code> at all. Members read only their own <code>memberProfiles/{memberId}</code>, an allowlist without <code>phoneLast4</code>, also written by <code>ingestMemberUpdate</code> (Phase C verification finding). Only the kiosk lookup function (<code>kioskLookup</code>) uses <code>phoneLast4</code>, and it returns just the first name and last initial, plus booking status.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:265:<tr><td>D23</td><td>Functions generation and locations</td><td><strong>2nd gen everywhere.</strong> Each project records <em>three</em> separate values:
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:271:  Also: explicit <code>maxInstances</code>, the Admin app built once per instance, an Artifact Registry cleanup policy, and <strong>retries set explicitly</strong> (<code>retry: true</code> on the triggers, <code>retryConfig</code> on the schedules; both are off by default).</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:274:<h3 id="iam">IAM inventory (D11). Christie makes the Console/IAM changes; each one is recorded in the resilience plan</h3>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:278:<tr><td>Both</td><td>APIs: <code>run</code>, <code>eventarc</code>, <code>cloudfunctions</code>, <code>cloudbuild</code>, <code>artifactregistry</code>, <code>pubsub</code>, <code>cloudscheduler</code>, <code>iamcredentials</code>. Wait for the service agents (<code>gcp-sa-eventarc</code>, the Cloud Functions agent) before the first deploy.</td><td>Needed by 2nd gen. A first deploy that fails while these are propagating isn't a real failure; retry it.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:279:<tr><td>Both</td><td><strong>Amended Sep 29 (M7):</strong> no dedicated build account — the Firebase CLI can't choose one (firebase-functions-deploy-guard K12); Google picks the Compute account or the legacy Cloud Build account. So <strong>both candidates are neutralized</strong> (no Editor, no <code>cloudbuild.builds.builder</code>), and only the account Google actually builds with holds the three build roles: Logs Writer; Artifact Registry Writer on the pre-created <code>gcf-artifacts</code> only; Storage Object Viewer conditioned to the function-source buckets. For <code>my-clay-hub</code> that's the Compute account (D2-1, Sep 29). <em>(Was: a dedicated build service account passed on deploy.)</em></td><td>Otherwise builds run as a default account holding broad roles.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:280:<tr><td>Both</td><td>The deployer (Christie's account, via the guard) holds <code>iam.serviceAccounts.actAs</code> on each <strong>runtime</strong> service account. <strong>Amended Sep 29 (M7):</strong> it comes from Christie's Owner role (recorded in D2-1); if Owner is ever narrowed, a Service Account User grant on each runtime account replaces it. There is no build account to act as.</td><td>Deploying as a chosen service account requires it.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:292:<p><strong>Palette (bright brand colours, Christie's choice):</strong> orange <code>#FF622D</code> · lavender <code>#CDAFD3</code> · sage <code>#999878</code> · peach <code>#F9D1AE</code> · cream <code>#F2EABE</code> · pink <code>#FFCAD4</code> · rust <code>#BB5C3C</code> · coral <code>#F6916D</code> · white, <strong>plus Tinker teal <code>#3DB9AF</code></strong> to tie the two brands together.</p>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:339:<p><strong>Order:</strong> A → C (docs, which can run alongside B) → B (on hold) → D → D2 → E → F (its own plan).</p>
