/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:527:<p class="note">Expanded into its own plan, <code>my-clay-hub-phase-d-project.html</code> (plan_MLuK0XL--VSd, Sep 28), which is the record. Amended there after review: <code>functions-build@</code> is created with no roles (Phase D2 grants them before any function deploy — <strong>superseded Sep 29 by M7: <code>functions-build@</code> was deleted in D2-1, since the CLI can't use it</strong>); the managed backup schedule is in D-1; the vault export runs after Phase D2 and gates Phase E's real data; bookings never cross midnight (C6).</p>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:530:  <li>The project exists on Blaze with a budget alert, server-side backups, the IAM baseline (the default service account has no Editor, the APIs are enabled, <code>functions-build@</code> exists with no roles — its roles and the deployer's <code>actAs</code> land in Phase D2 before any function deploy. <strong>Amended Sep 29 (M7):</strong> <code>functions-build@</code> was deleted in D2-1; the build roles went to the account Google actually builds with, and the deployer's <code>actAs</code> on each runtime account comes from Christie's Owner role) and a deliberate database location.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:541:      <li>create Firestore in the D23 location, and Storage;</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:553:  <li><strong>D-4:</strong> the vault export (D13) — <strong>after Phase D2</strong>, as a scheduled function that waits for each export to finish. <strong>Amended Sep 29 (M6):</strong> Phase D2's guard is HTTP-only, so D-4's own plan must first extend it with scheduled functions — a real Cloud Scheduler read-back, <code>retryConfig</code>, and its own review — before the export function ships. The managed backup schedule moved to D-1. <strong>Phase E loads no real member data until the first vault export has completed successfully.</strong></li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:569:<h3>Phase D2 — A functions-aware deploy guard (its own plan) <span class="status-tag ready">own plan, execution-ready (Sep 29)</span></h3>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:570:<p>Its own plan (<code>firebase-functions-deploy-guard.html</code>, plan_a_Hq4YGUE5Hq, extending <code>firebase-deploy-guard.html</code>) delivers the list below. <strong>Amendments M1–M7, approved by Christie Sep 29, are shown inline</strong>; the D2 plan's Amendments table has the reasons. Scope (Christie, Sep 29): <code>my-clay-hub</code> only, HTTP functions only, Node 22.</p>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:571:<p><em>Originally "for both projects". <strong>M1:</strong> each project gets its own, separate guard — <code>my-clay-hub</code>'s now; <code>tinker-hq-apps</code>' copy at the start of Phase E, when the <code>clayhub-link</code> code exists. Neither guard can ever reach the other project.</em></p>
