/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:670:<p>Findings: Membership Manager save safety; email-derived identity; event ordering; overly broad IAM; the <code>backup.js</code> credential; the guard not handling functions; A2 and A5 safety; D1, D3 and D4 gaps; retries, generation and region; reconcile safety; the <code>staffRoster</code> dependency; D-1 ordering; the A3 line range; the Booking footprint; Phase C's decision coverage. All were verified and addressed in the round-1 revision.</p>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:674:<tr><td>The email-change handover breaks single-version ordering; deletes have no update time; equal timestamps (both)</td><td><strong>D22 redesigned:</strong> "re-read, then send a snapshot". Each message is the full truth for a <code>memberId</code> at its read time. Plus the conflict rule and ordering tests in both directions.</td></tr>
