/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html:764:  <li><strong>Sep 28: ✅ Phase B complete</strong> — executed as its own plan <code>clay-hub-membership-save-safety.html</code> (plan_7qlaYjlmpAHf; its Decisions log is the full record). All live on Render at <code>c3d2f7c</code>: B1 honest saves, B0 rules (tinker-hq-apps <code>e572a09</code>, receipt <code>deployed/tinker-hq-apps/firestore-rules/20260928T050431Z-e572a09</code>: a set <code>memberId</code> can't change, <code>retired</code> docs frozen), B3 permanent <code>memberId</code> (Christie ran the backfill: 66 assigned; verified 66/66 valid + unique in the 16:27Z backup), B5 prior-term pauses + 3 months from rejoining, B2 editable phone. <strong>B4 (change email) is deferred to its own plan</strong>; D22's link already tolerates retired docs. Every step had a Codex + Claude review. For Phase E: every member doc now carries <code>memberId</code>; the link must still never copy the exclusion list in the save-safety plan ("What My Clay Hub's link needs"); residual noted there — a manager can delete + re-create a member doc with a new <code>memberId</code> (create is unrestricted), so the link should treat a changed memberId for an email as a new member. <strong>Next: Phase D</strong> (create the <code>my-clay-hub</code> Firebase project; show Christie the D-3 CLAUDE.md "exactly two projects" wording first).</li>
