/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:54:<p>Read from the pinned tools in this repo (firebase-tools <strong>15.22.3</strong>, firebase-functions <strong>7.4.0</strong>) or from Google's docs on Oct 1, and checked by both round-1 reviewers. "Verify" means a phase step proves it before anything depends on it.</p>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:57:<tr><td>J1</td><td><code>functions:list</code> shows a scheduled v2 function only as <code>scheduleTrigger: {}</code> plus the label <code>deployment-scheduled: "true"</code> (<code>gcp/cloudfunctionsv2.js:299-305</code>; labels are copied through). Schedule, time zone, retry settings, deadline and target are not visible to the CLI.</td><td>The Scheduler job is read by Christie and checked by the script (V2). The guard can't prove the schedule; it proves her reading matches (V2).</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:61:<tr><td>J5</td><td>The job is only patched when schedule, time zone, deadline or retry changed; retry is compared with a <strong>partial</strong> match, so live retry fields not in the code are neither cleared nor noticed (<code>cloudscheduler.js:82-108</code>). The job is created/patched <strong>after</strong> the function (<code>fabricator.js:161, 182</code>): a failed job upsert leaves a live function with no (or an old) job and a non-zero exit. Removing a schedule from code orphans the job: it keeps POSTing.</td><td>V3 requires all five retry values; V2 reads the whole job; the runbook covers each partial state.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:62:<tr><td>J6</td><td>onSchedule pre-fills <code>timeZone</code> and all five retry keys with a reset marker that serialises to <code>null</code> (<code>runtime/manifest.js:32-45, 113-135</code>), so an unset field is <em>present</em> as <code>null</code>. <code>requiredAPIs</code> is a list of <code>{api, reason}</code> objects: <code>[{api: "cloudscheduler.googleapis.com", reason: …}]</code>. The handler's <code>event.scheduleTime</code> is the <code>X-CloudScheduler-ScheduleTime</code> header, or now if absent; a thrown error is logged with <code>logger.error</code> and answered 500; the wrapper writes the response itself (<code>v2/providers/scheduler.js:42-66</code>).</td><td>V3 checks numbers and the string <code>"UTC"</code>, not presence; O6.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:67:<tr><td>J11</td><td>Scheduler: <code>retryCount</code> 0–5 — retried that many times "or until the next scheduled execution, whichever first"; <code>maxRetryDuration</code> 0 = unlimited, and when both are set it retries until <em>both</em> limits are reached. A late response is cancelled as <code>DEADLINE_EXCEEDED</code>; whether the Cloud Run request keeps running is undocumented.</td><td>V6 (<code>maxRetrySeconds: 0</code>), V7 (own wait budget).</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:71:<tr><td>J15</td><td>Cloud Scheduler: the <code>X-CloudScheduler-ScheduleTime</code> header "contains the original scheduled invocation time and remains constant across retry attempts" (<a href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/scheduler/docs/creating">Manage cron jobs</a>).</td><td>V7's key (the date of the scheduled time) is the same for a run and all its retries.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:72:<tr><td>J16</td><td><strong>Undocumented:</strong> when Google creates the Firestore service agent, and whether a PERMISSION_DENIED from an export names the principal. Documented: its address form, <code>service-&lt;PROJECT_NUMBER&gt;@gcp-sa-firestore.iam.gserviceaccount.com</code> (project number 760301318440), and that a bucket in another project needs an explicit grant.</td><td>V-4 step 7 has a written branch for each case.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:79:<tr><td>V2</td><td><strong>The Scheduler read-back is Christie's Console reading, checked by the script.</strong> <code>--attest</code> evidence gains two keys, <strong>always present</strong>, for every codebase: <code>schedulerJobList</code> (every job name in <code>us-central1</code>, a complete list, as the Console shows it) and <code>schedulerJobs</code> (one entry per scheduled function <em>of this codebase</em>: name, state, schedule, timeZone, targetUri, httpMethod, oidcServiceAccount, oidcAudience, body, headers, attemptDeadline and the five retry values). The script requires:
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:84:  <strong>Transcription format</strong> (like role ids): durations as whole seconds, numbers not text — <code>attemptDeadline: 1800</code>, <code>retryCount: 3</code>, <code>maxRetrySeconds: 0</code>, <code>minBackoffSeconds: 600</code>, <code>maxBackoffSeconds: 3600</code>, <code>maxDoublings: 2</code> — whatever the Console displays ("30m", "10m"); the template says so.<br>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:87:<tr><td>V3</td><td><strong>The guard's rules for a schedule</strong> (F13 amended for schedules only):
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:89:  <li>a declaration's <strong>key set is exact</strong>: HTTP <code>{trigger: "https", serviceAccount, invoker, ingress}</code>; schedule <code>{trigger: "schedule", serviceAccount, ingress, schedule: {schedule, timeZone, retryCount, maxRetrySeconds, minBackoffSeconds, maxBackoffSeconds, maxDoublings}}</code>. Any unknown or missing key refuses by name.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:91:  <li><code>scheduleTrigger</code>'s <code>schedule</code> and <code>timeZone</code> are strings and its five retry values are <strong>numbers</strong>, each equal to the declaration (J6: <code>null</code> means "unset" and refuses); <code>timeZone</code> must be <code>"UTC"</code>;</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:99:  <li>The Firestore service agent: <code>projects/tinker-hq-vault/roles/firestoreExportWriter</code> (the four J8 permissions) on the vault bucket only, granted in V-4 (bootstrap).</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:102:  Admin clients are built with explicit project and database names (no project discovery). <code>actAs</code> comes from Christie's Owner role (M7). Any widening needs the exact denied permission from a real error and Christie's approval.</td><td>Parent D-4. The two <code>tinker-hq-vault</code> grants can't be read by <code>--attest</code> (it reads only <code>my-clay-hub</code>'s IAM); V-1/V-4 screenshots plus V-4/V-5 behaviour are their record.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:104:<tr><td>V6</td><td><strong><code>vaultExport</code> limits:</strong> <code>retryCount: 3</code>, <code>maxRetrySeconds: 0</code>, <code>minBackoffSeconds: 600</code>, <code>maxBackoffSeconds: 3600</code>, <code>maxDoublings: 2</code> → retries about 10, 20 and 40 min after each failed attempt ends, then stop (J11; observed in V-4). A fast failure finishes the series in about 1¼ h; attempts that each run to the 1,500 s budget stretch it to about 2¾ h. <code>timeoutSeconds: 1800</code>, <code>maxInstances: 1</code>, <code>concurrency: 1</code>, <code>cpu: 1</code>, <code>memory: 512MiB</code>, <code>ingressSettings: ALLOW_ALL</code> (as the canary; Scheduler calls the public URL with a token).</td><td>A failed Sunday run gets three more tries the same morning. 512 MiB is cheap headroom for the gRPC admin client.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:108:  <li><strong>Running already?</strong> List this database's operations (<code>listOperationsAsync</code> on <code>projects/my-clay-hub/databases/(default)</code>, paged, filtered client-side to exports whose prefix starts <code>gs://&lt;bucket&gt;/weekly/D-</code>; <strong>cap: 1,000 operations examined</strong>, and hitting it throws — never "none"). A listed operation's <code>metadata</code> is a raw <code>google.protobuf.Any</code> (Firestore 9.3.0 <code>firestore_admin_v1_proto_api.d.ts:10355</code>): it is decoded with the pinned protobuf <strong>only</strong> when its type URL is exactly <code>type.googleapis.com/google.firestore.admin.v1.ExportDocumentsMetadata</code>, and the numeric <code>operationState</code> is mapped to its name. An operation with another type URL is not an export and is skipped; export metadata that fails to decode, or has an unknown state, throws (never treated as "not ours"). One not done → wait on it. One done <code>SUCCESSFUL</code> but no complete folder → throw (inconsistent: needs a person). Ones done <code>FAILED</code>/<code>CANCELLED</code> (or with <code>error</code>) are history: logged, never resumed, and their prefixes never reused → go to step 3. (This is V-4's bootstrap path.)</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:111:  Waiting polls every 15 s with a <strong>budget of 1,500 s from the start of the run</strong>; on expiry it throws ("still running; the retry resumes"), so the error path and alert always run before Cloud Run's 1,800 s kill. Success needs: <code>done</code>, no <code>error</code>, state <code>SUCCESSFUL</code>, the expected prefix, and the complete folder visible in the bucket. Anything else throws.<br>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:112:  <strong>Duplicates:</strong> two runs racing within seconds, or a lost reply that Google hasn't listed by the next retry, can each start an export. Each goes to its own prefix, so the result is two complete copies. At most one export per invocation, and at most 4 invocations per scheduled run. A Force run on another day gets its own key (an honest extra copy).<br>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:113:  <strong>State</strong> is the bucket (durable for 56 days) plus the operation list (used only for "still running", which is well inside its few-day retention). No Firestore collection, so <code>vault-export@</code> never gets data access.</td><td>Both round-1 reviews: the operation list alone can't be the record, and <code>maxInstances</code> isn't a lock. Christie chose (Oct 1) to allow a rare second copy rather than build a lock.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:121:<tr><td>V14</td><td><strong>Restore runbook</strong> <code>docs/my-clay-hub/DATA-RESTORE.md</code>: choose the newest <strong>complete</strong> folder (its metadata file present and named after it — lifecycle deletes folders gradually, so a folder can be half there); the temporary read grant (<code>storage.buckets.get</code> + <code>storage.objects.get</code>) for the <em>importing</em> database's Firestore service agent, removed afterwards; an import <strong>overwrites matching documents and deletes nothing</strong>, so into a non-empty database it is a merge, not a rollback. The rehearsal happens in Phase E (O3).</td><td>Parent D-4.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:129:<tr><td>O3</td><td>Rehearse a restore now or after Phase E?</td><td>After Phase E (real data); added to Phase E's checklist in V-6.</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:131:<tr><td>O5</td><td>Strict lock or allow a rare second copy?</td><td><strong>Allow a rare second copy</strong> (V7): each run writes to its own folder, so the worst case is two complete copies, never a mixed one. Changes the outline's "retries never make a second export" to "a retry never starts a second export when the first is visible".</td></tr>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:136:<p>Order: <strong>V-0 → V-1 → V-2 → V-3 → V-4 → V-5 → V-6</strong>. V-0/V-1 (Console) and V-2 (guard code) can run in parallel. V-3 needs V-0's Monitoring agent address (for <code>vaultFresh</code>'s declared invoker) and V-1's bucket name, so it can't finish before them. V-2 and V-3 are each one branch and one PR, reviewed (Codex + Claude), then merged. Nothing is released before V-4.</p>
