/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:431:  <li><strong>Oct 1, V-0 steps 4–8, 10–11 (and step 6):</strong> ✅ Import/Export page: "Import/Export jobs run as: <code>service-760301318440@gcp-sa-firestore.iam.gserviceaccount.com</code>" (= the IAM row); no exports yet. Custom role <code>projects/my-clay-hub/roles/vaultExporter</code> ("Vault exporter", GA) created with exactly <code>datastore.databases.export</code>, <code>datastore.operations.get</code>, <code>datastore.operations.list</code> (picked from the Import Export Admin role's list; <code>databases.import</code> left out; screenshot of the 3 assigned permissions). Service accounts <code>vault-export@</code> and <code>vault-watch@my-clay-hub.iam.gserviceaccount.com</code> created, enabled, no keys. Project grant: Vault exporter → <code>vault-export@</code> only. Email channel "Christie — My Clay Hub alerts" (<code>Christie@tinkerartstudio.com</code>) created; <strong>the Console offers no test button for email channels</strong>, so its first email is proven by V-4's deliberate failure (already required there). <strong>After-reading:</strong> identical to step 1 plus exactly one new row, Vault exporter (1) → <code>vault-export@</code>; Editor still only the Google APIs Service Agent; no new Google agent rows. <strong>V-0 complete</strong> — no Google agent grants to add to <code>iam-expectations.json</code>.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:432:  <li><strong>Oct 1, V-2 (in progress, branch <code>d4-guard-schedules</code>):</strong> step 1 proved offline and in the emulator (new session 3, <code>tests/functions/fixtures/schedule-probe</code>): the emulator loads a codebase holding an <code>onSchedule</code> (it skips the schedule — no Pub/Sub emulator — and serves the HTTP function beside it); firebase-functions 7.4.0's wire manifest is exactly J6's shape. <strong>J6 correction:</strong> a retry value or time zone left out of the code is <em>absent</em> from <code>scheduleTrigger</code>, not <code>null</code> (top-level options are <code>null</code>); V3's "a number equal to the declaration" refuses both, and both are tested. A scheduled function's live env is the same five keys (prepare.js sets <code>EVENTARC_CLOUD_EVENT_SOURCE</code> for every v2 endpoint). The plan's note that <code>tests/unit/test-scripts.test.js</code> asserts <code>CODEBASE_MODULES</code> was wrong (it doesn't); <code>functions-emulator.test.js</code> does, and is updated.</li>
