/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:436:  <li><strong>Oct 2, V-1 (Christie in the Console; readings by screenshot, the "after" readings read by Claude in Christie's Chrome, read-only):</strong> ✅ <strong>Bucket name: <code>my-clay-hub-vault-exports</code></strong> (first choice was free) in <code>tinker-hq-vault</code>, created Oct 2 2026 1:01:40 PM UTC-6: Multi-region <code>us</code>, Standard, cross-bucket replication off, hierarchical namespace off, Uniform, public access prevention enforced (not public), soft delete 7 days, versioning Off, retention None / object retention Disabled, Google-managed encryption. Lifecycle: exactly one rule, Delete object at 56+ days since creation, no scope; no day-less second rule appeared. Custom roles in <code>tinker-hq-vault</code> (GA, Enabled): <code>projects/tinker-hq-vault/roles/firestoreExportWriter</code> = storage.buckets.get, storage.objects.create, storage.objects.delete, storage.objects.list; <code>projects/tinker-hq-vault/roles/vaultLister</code> = storage.objects.list. Bucket grant: Vault lister → <code>vault-export@</code> and <code>vault-watch@my-clay-hub.iam.gserviceaccount.com</code> — saved without error (no domain-restricted-sharing refusal). The new bucket's Permissions = those two plus the default rows every bucket gets (four inherited Tinker HQ Vault service agents; Storage Legacy Bucket/Object Owner → project Editors + Owners; Legacy Bucket/Object Reader → project Viewers) — identical in shape to the staff bucket. No grant to the Firestore agent (V-4). <strong>Before/after:</strong> <code>tinker-hq-vault-backups</code> Configuration identical field by field (us-central1, Standard, Uniform, PAP on, soft delete 7 d, versioning Off, retention None, lifecycle None, Updated still Aug 11 2026 11:59:23 AM) and Permissions identical (the same 8 role rows, same members); <code>tinker-hq-vault</code> project IAM (Google-provided grants included) identical: Firebase Admin SDK Administrator Service Agent, Firebase Rules System, Firebase Service Management Service Agent, Firestore Service Agent, Owner (Christie), Service Account Token Creator — 1 member each. No project-level grant was made. V-1 complete.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:437:  <li><strong>Oct 2, V-3 built on <code>d4-vault-codebase</code> (<code>1053127</code>, not pushed yet):</strong> <code>functions/vault/</code> per V1 (index, export-run, freshness, vault-bucket, clients, vault-config, reached), declarations (vaultExport schedule; vaultFresh https, invoker = the Monitoring agent from V-0 step 7), iam-expectations (vault-export@ &rarr; vaultExporter; vault-watch@ &rarr; none), firebase.json entry; DATA-RESTORE.md; DECISIONS #63. <strong>Deviation:</strong> direct dependency <code>@google-cloud/firestore-api</code> 0.2.0 instead of <code>@google-cloud/firestore</code>: in Firestore 9.3.0 the v1 admin client and its generated protos live there (same resolved copy; the lockfile's package set is identical to core's). Found while building: (1) over gRPC a listed or fetched Operation's Any keeps the field name <code>type_url</code> (proto-loader special-cases Any), and a failed operation may carry no metadata; test fixtures are encoded with the pinned protos and decoded with proto-loader using google-gax's options. (2) The emulator lists vaultExport (as a pubsub trigger with its schedule) but skips it; vaultFresh is served, and clients.js refuses real clients there (500 in about 0.4 s, nothing reaches Google). (3) With two codebases in firebase.json, the backstop's M5 RESOURCE_DIR refusal now fires for real on <code>--only functions</code> and on a mistyped <code>functions:&lt;function id&gt;</code> (tests updated to expect it). (4) The guard's own JQ_MANIFEST passes vault's discovered manifest with no reasons. Mutation checks: 15 refusals or branches broken in turn, each caught (one gap found and closed: an object whose name merely starts with the metadata file's name). Tests: unit 228, rules guard 196, functions guard 877, emulator 48+2+3, rules 194. Implementation review round 1 (Codex + Claude) running.</li>
/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:438:  <li><strong>Oct 2, V-3 implementation review round 1:</strong> Codex "merge after fixes" (2 blocking, 1 should-fix, 1 nit); Claude "merge after fixes" (5 should-fix, 6 nits). All applied except where noted: <strong>every call to Google is now held to the run's budget</strong> (new <code>deadline.js</code>: each call gets only the time left, and the client is passed the same timeout), so a stuck call can't carry a run past Cloud Run's kill (both reviewers; the fakes now model hung and slow calls); no export is started with under 5 min of budget left; <code>vaultFresh</code>'s listings get 20 s in all, so it always answers before its 30 s timeout; an unknown export state is judged only for exports of the run's own date (Claude); a fresh suffix never repeats a folder or prefix already seen (Claude); a page cap on folder listings (Claude); tests for the reachable "finished between the two listings" branch, the bucket reader's defensive branches, and <code>vaultExport</code>'s real wiring with only clients.js faked (Claude). DATA-RESTORE.md: the pre-restore copy is a manual Console export to <code>manual/pre-restore-&lt;date&gt;</code>, verified by its metadata file, never a Force run (both); a permission refusal stops for Christie's approval instead of widening (Codex); a scratch database is created deny-all (Claude). DECISIONS #63: only Christie, by hand, can import (Codex). V-4 gains the check above (Claude). <strong>Not changed:</strong> <code>firebase-admin</code> stays a direct dependency: it is a required peer dependency of firebase-functions 7.4.0 (npm would install it regardless), and V1 names it (Claude nit 10).</li>
