/Users/christiehubley/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/my-clay-hub-d4-vault-export.html:450:  <li><strong>Oct 7, finding — a Force run takes the NEXT scheduled time:</strong> the start line read <code>scheduleTime "2026-10-11T02:00:00-07:00"</code>, <code>key "2026-10-11"</code> on a Wednesday. The V7 tests assumed a Force run arrives without the header. A weekday Force run would therefore take the coming Sunday's key and that Sunday's real run would skip ("already done"), then the freshness alarm would fire. Christie: don't hold V-4 — grant after the retries end and let Sunday Oct 11's scheduled run make the first export; fix the key next, before Phase E; until then <strong>no Force run at all</strong>. Fix drafted on branch <code>d4-force-run-key</code> (<code>884d5f2</code>): a scheduled time still in the future is keyed by today's UTC date; a new test fails on the old code; DECISIONS #64; FUNCTIONS-ROLLBACK §10 and DATA-RESTORE.md updated. V-4 step 9 ("Force run again: already done") moves to after that fix ships.</li>
