   191	<tr><td>D4</td><td>What decides a member's status</td><td>A single tested function, <code>deriveStatus(source, todayDenver)</code>. It uses Denver calendar dates and parses <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code> strings as dates, never through <code>new Date()</code>. It runs <strong>inside <code>ingestMemberUpdate</code></strong> on every write (Phase E), and again for everyone at <strong>3:30 AM Denver</strong> daily (Phase E; this avoids the DST gap). Rules are applied in order; the first match wins:
   192	  <ol>
   193	    <li>No live source record (tombstoned) → <code>removed</code> (no access)</li>
   194	    <li><code>stage</code> is <code>onboarding</code> or <code>touring</code> → <code>not_yet</code> (no access)</li>
   195	    <li><code>stage</code> is missing, or isn't one of the six known values → <code>review</code></li>
   196	    <li><code>finalAccessDate</code> is present but malformed → <code>review</code>. If valid and <strong>today is after it</strong> → <code>offboarded</code>. <em>The last day itself still has access.</em></li>
   197	    <li><code>stage:'cancelled'</code> with no <code>finalAccessDate</code> → <code>offboarded</code></li>
   198	    <li><code>stage:'offboarding'</code> with no <code>finalAccessDate</code> → <code>review</code></li>
   199	    <li>Any pause window (in <code>scheduledPause</code> or <em>any</em> <code>pauseHistory</code> entry, either spelling) with a missing or malformed date → <code>review</code></li>
   200	    <li>Any valid pause window with <strong>start ≤ today ≤ end</strong> (both days included; D4a) → <code>paused</code></li>
   201	    <li><code>stage:'paused'</code> with no pause windows at all → <code>review</code></li>
   202	    <li>Otherwise → <code>active</code>. That covers <code>active</code>, a <code>paused</code> stage whose window has ended, <code>offboarding</code> before the last day, and <code>cancelled</code> with a future last day.</li>
   203	  </ol>
   204	  <strong>Sign-in allowed:</strong> <code>active</code>, <code>paused</code>, <code>review</code>. <strong>Booking allowed:</strong> <code>active</code> only. <strong><code>review</code></strong> means booking is locked, the member sees "We're checking your membership details — you can still see the feed", and staff see a flag. Where this disagrees with Membership Manager's own <code>stage</code>, <code>deriveStatus</code> wins.</td></tr>
