   289	<h3 id="brand">Brand (D20)</h3>
   290	<div class="decision">
   291	<p><strong>Source:</strong> Christie's Clay Hub brand sheet and logo SVGs, committed at <code>my-clay-hub/docs/my-clay-hub/brand/</code>.</p>
   292	<p><strong>Palette (bright brand colours, Christie's choice):</strong> orange <code>#FF622D</code> · lavender <code>#CDAFD3</code> · sage <code>#999878</code> · peach <code>#F9D1AE</code> · cream <code>#F2EABE</code> · pink <code>#FFCAD4</code> · rust <code>#BB5C3C</code> · coral <code>#F6916D</code> · white, <strong>plus Tinker teal <code>#3DB9AF</code></strong> to tie the two brands together.</p>
   293	<p><strong>Readability comes first</strong> (Christie). Shades adjusted for readability are pre-approved, as long as she's told.</p>
   294	<ul>
   295	  <li><strong>Measured contrast:</strong> no brand colour is readable as small text on cream (rust is closest at 4.4:1). Dark text works on all of them.</li>
   575	  <li>a receipt recording the commit plus the folder hash, and a post-release read-back of each function's revision <strong>and its invoker policy</strong> (it fails if <code>allUsers</code> appears on <code>ingestmemberupdate</code>). <strong>M2:</strong> the CLI can't read a revision id; the guard reads back the full configuration, the env keys, and the content hash, and Christie reads the revision (Cloud Run → latest ready revision; Cloud Build build id) in a fixed shape the script validates. <strong>M3:</strong> without gcloud, Christie reads each function's Security tab and Permissions plus the project-level IAM list; <code>--attest</code> records that and the script computes the match against the declarations. Folder and organization grants stay unverifiable;</li>
   576	  <li>a clear record when a deploy only partly succeeds;</li>
   577	  <li>the functions emulator tests run first;</li>
   578	  <li><code>--only functions:&lt;codebase&gt;</code>, with a check that the name is a codebase and not a single function.</li>
   579	</ul>
   580	</div>
   581	
   582	<div class="phase" id="phase-e">
   583	<h3>Phase E — The live link from Membership Manager <span class="status-tag not-ready">execution-ready: false — needs B, D, D2, and the post-D2 vault export (one successful export before any real member data)</span></h3>
   584	<p><strong>Acceptance criteria:</strong></p>
   585	<ul>
   586	  <li>When staff add, edit, pause, offboard or change the email of a member, <code>members/{memberId}</code> matches within a minute, <strong>including its derived status</strong>.</li>
   587	  <li>Events arriving late, twice or out of order, deletes, and email changes (in either delivery order) always end with one correct live projection.</li>
   588	  <li>Two live source docs for one <code>memberId</code> trigger an alert, and nothing changes.</li>
   589	  <li>The reconcile runs every 6 hours, and the status recompute daily at 3:30 AM.</li>
   590	  <li>A reconcile that can't read the complete source changes nothing and alerts. A run that would change more than 10% of statuses, or remove more than 5% of members, stops and alerts.</li>
   591	  <li><code>staffRoster</code> holds only explicit grants. Unticking takes effect within a minute.</li>
   592	  <li><strong>An unauthenticated request to <code>ingestMemberUpdate</code> gets a 403.</strong> The link can invoke it, and can't write to either database.</li>
   593	</ul>
