     1	# Data model (Firestore)
     2	
     3	Decided in the foundation plan (`~/tinker-ai-configs/thoughts/plans/clayhub-members-foundation.html`) after inspecting the
     4	real Membership Manager and Tinker HQ code (Sep 25–27, 2026). The decision numbers (#30…) refer to `DECISIONS.md`. Collection
     5	and field names here are the plan of record. Change them only through a new decision.
     6	
     7	## Two Firebase projects (#30)
     8	
     9	| Project | Who signs in | What lives here |
    10	|---|---|---|
    11	| `tinker-hq-apps` | Staff only (email/password) | Every internal Tinker app, including **Membership Manager** (`clayHub_members`) and Tinker HQ (`users`). My Clay Hub adds **nothing** here except the `clayhub-link` functions. |
    12	| `my-clay-hub` | Members (magic link, Google), staff via `/staff` (exchanged Tinker HQ login), the kiosk account | Everything below. Its own rules (`my-clay-hub/firestore.rules`), its own guard. |
    13	
    14	Nothing in `my-clay-hub` can read or write `tinker-hq-apps`. Members never get an account in `tinker-hq-apps`.
    15	
    16	## Where member data comes from (source, read-only)
    17	
    18	`tinker-hq-apps` → `clayHub_members/{docId}`. This is Membership Manager's collection, and it's **never written by this app** (#37).
    19	
    20	- **Doc ID:** the email lowercased, with `.` and `/` replaced by `_`. It isn't unique (`a.b@x.com` and `a_b@x.com` collide), so it's never used as an identity.
    21	- **`memberId`:** a permanent random ID, added by Membership Manager in plan Phase B (#52). **This is the identity everywhere in My Clay Hub.**
    22	- **`retired: true`:** set on the old doc when staff change a member's email (Phase B). Live means `retired !== true`.
    23	- **`name`:** one string (there's no first/last split). **`email`:** original case. **`phone`:** free text (blank for some Sawyer imports).
    24	- **`stage`:** `onboarding | touring | active | paused | offboarding | cancelled`. It's only brought up to date when someone opens Membership Manager.
    25	- **Pause dates**, in `YYYY-MM-DD` strings:
    26	  - `scheduledPause.startDate` / `.endDate`;
    27	  - `pauseHistory[]` entries, which use **either** `startDate`/`endDate` **or** the legacy `start`/`end`.
    28	- **Last day:** `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`).
    29	- **`memberSince`:** added in Phase B (#36).
    30	
    31	`tinker-hq-apps` → `users/{uid}` (Tinker HQ staff): `role`, `appAccess[]`, `active`. Read by the link to build the staff roster.
    32	
    33	## The one-way link (#53)
    34	
    35	1. A 2nd-gen trigger in `tinker-hq-apps` (`clayhub-link`) fires when a `clayHub_members` doc changes. It collects the `memberId` from the before **and** after versions.
    36	2. For each `memberId`, it runs **one query filtered on `memberId` only**, and decides live/retired in memory. The query's `readTime` is the snapshot time.
    37	   - exactly one live doc → a snapshot of that doc's allowed fields;
    38	   - no live doc → a tombstone;
    39	   - **more than one live doc → a conflict:** nothing is sent, and it alerts.
    40	3. It POSTs `{memberId, snapshot, readTime}` to the private HTTPS function `ingestMemberUpdate` in `my-clay-hub`, using its own service account's identity token.
    41	4. `ingestMemberUpdate`, in a transaction:
    42	   - rejects the payload unless it's strictly valid;
    43	   - **ignores it unless `readTime` is later than the stored `sourceReadTime`** (a member with no stored time accepts anything);
    44	   - runs `deriveStatus`, and writes `members/{memberId}`;
    45	   - **never deletes**; a tombstone is a flag.
    46	
    47	- **Staff roster:** `users/{uid}` changes flow the same way into `staffRoster/staff_{uid}`, using that document read's `readTime`. Only people with an explicit grant are projected: active, and a manager or admin role, or `appAccess` containing `my-clay-hub`.
    48	- **Reconcile:** every 6 hours. It reads the whole source in **one read-only transaction pinned to a single `readTime`**, then sends every member (and tombstone) through the same `ingestMemberUpdate` gate.
    49	  - If the read is incomplete, it changes nothing and alerts.
    50	  - If a run would change more than 10% of statuses, or tombstone more than 5% of members, it stops and alerts.
    51	- `sourceReadTime` is a `tinker-hq-apps` timestamp. It's only ever compared with other `tinker-hq-apps` read times.
    52	
    53	**Copied fields only:** `name`, `firstName`, `lastInitial` (worked out from `name`), `email` (original case, for display), `emailLower` (for matching), `stage`, the pause windows (both spellings normalized), `finalAccessDate`, `memberSince`, and **`phoneLast4`**, worked out in `tinker-hq-apps`. The full phone number never leaves that project (#24).
    54	
    55	## `deriveStatus(source, todayDenver)` (#34, #35)
    56	
    57	Code: `shared/derive-status.js`, using `shared/denver-time.js`. These are the only status and date code: `ingestMemberUpdate` and
    58	the 3:30 AM recompute import them, and nothing re-derives status elsewhere. `todayDenver` is passed in, never read from the clock inside.
    59	
    60	Denver calendar dates only. `YYYY-MM-DD` strings are compared as dates, never through `new Date()`. A date must be strictly
    61	`YYYY-MM-DD` and a real day (no `2026-02-30`, no other shapes); anything else is **malformed**. The rules below run in order; the first match wins.
    62	
    63	1. No live source record (tombstone) → **`removed`**
    64	2. `stage` is `onboarding` or `touring` → **`not_yet`**
    65	3. `stage` is missing, or isn't one of the six known values → **`review`**
    66	4. `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate`:
    67	   - present but malformed → **`review`**;
    68	   - valid, and today is **after** it → **`offboarded`**. The last day itself still has access.
    69	5. `stage: 'cancelled'` with no `finalAccessDate` → **`offboarded`**
    70	6. `stage: 'offboarding'` with no `finalAccessDate` → **`review`**
    71	7. Any pause window (in `scheduledPause` or any `pauseHistory` entry, either spelling) that is **missing, malformed, or reversed** (its end is before its start) → **`review`** (C8). A one-day pause (start = end) is valid. A pause with a start but **no end
    72	   date** is `review` too, never "paused indefinitely" (#59): staff see the flag and add the end date, and the pause's booking
    73	   cancellation happens then (a window with no end gives nothing to cancel against).
    74	8. Any valid pause window with **start ≤ today ≤ end** (both days included) → **`paused`**
    75	9. `stage: 'paused'` with no pause windows at all → **`review`**
    76	10. Otherwise → **`active`**. That covers `active`, a paused stage whose window has ended, `offboarding` before the last day, and `cancelled` with a future last day.
    77	
    78	How the code reads the edges of these rules (D-5):
    79	- Rule 1 also treats a record with `retired: true` as no live record, since live means `retired !== true`.
    80	- A cleared pause or cancellation is `null` in Membership Manager, and counts as absent. A `scheduledCancellation` without a
    81	  `finalAccessDate` (`null` or missing) means no last day. Any other `finalAccessDate`, **including an empty string**, must be a
    82	  valid date or it's malformed (rule 4 → `review`).
    83	- A pause entry uses `startDate`/`endDate` when they're set, else the legacy `start`/`end`.
    84	- A source that isn't a record at all gives `review`. `deriveStatus` never throws on member data; it throws only if `todayDenver`
    85	  itself isn't a valid date (a caller bug). Supported dates are 1900–2999.
    86	- **Input shape:** `deriveStatus` reads the `clayHub_members` field shape (`stage`, `scheduledPause`, `pauseHistory`,
    87	  `scheduledCancellation.finalAccessDate`). Whatever `members/*` stores, `ingestMemberUpdate` and the 3:30 AM recompute must
    88	  hand it that shape. A flattened record would silently read as "no pause, no last day". Phase E tests that round trip.
    89	- **Deliberate differences from Membership Manager**, where it reads the same fields differently:
    90	  - A missing `stage` is `review` here (rule 3). Membership Manager treats it as active.
    91	  - Waitlisted and deferred people are stored as `stage: 'cancelled'`, so they derive to `offboarded`, not `not_yet`. Neither
    92	    can sign in, so the outcome is the same; it means `offboarded` isn't only former members.
    93	- As a check, run against the Sep 28, 2026 backup of all 66 `clayHub_members` records: every date was strict `YYYY-MM-DD`, and
    94	  none came out as `review`.
    95	
    96	| Status | Can sign in | Can book | Notes |
    97	|---|---|---|---|
    98	| `active` | yes | yes | |
    99	| `paused` | yes | no | Feed, What's on and My time are visible. The paused message names the day booking reopens (end + 1). |
   100	| `review` | yes | no | "We're checking your membership details — you can still see the feed." Staff see a flag. |
   101	| `offboarded`, `not_yet`, `removed` | no | no | `enforceMemberStatus` removes the claim, revokes sessions, and disables offboarded accounts (never deletes them). |
   102	
   103	It runs inside `ingestMemberUpdate` on every write, and again for everyone at **3:30 AM Denver** daily.
   104	
   105	## Collections in `my-clay-hub`
   106	
   107	`members/{memberId}`: the projection. It's written **only** by `ingestMemberUpdate`.
   108	- The copied fields above, plus `status`, `sourceReadTime`, `tombstone`, `updatedAt`.
   109	- **No client can read it**, not even the member themselves: Firestore rules can't hide single fields, and it holds `phoneLast4` (#24). Functions and rules read it on the server.
   110	
   111	`memberProfiles/{memberId}`: the **member-readable view**, written only by `ingestMemberUpdate` alongside `members`. It holds an allowlist only: `firstName`, `name`, `email`, `status`, `memberSince`, the current or next pause window (for the paused message), and `finalAccessDate`. **Never `phoneLast4`.** A member can read only their own.
   112	
   113	`staffRoster/staff_{uid}`: `{ name, role, active, grant }`, written only by `ingestMemberUpdate`. **No client can read it**; rules and functions check it.
   114	
   115	`settings/app`: a single doc, editable by managers and admins (#50).
   116	- `areas`: `[{ id: 'glaze', name: 'Glaze station', capacity: 4 }, { id: 'wheels', name: 'Wheels', capacity: 10 }, { id: 'handbuilding', name: 'Handbuilding table', capacity: 6 }]`. The 10 wheels include the 2 standing wheels, which aren't a separate area (#8).
   117	- `openTime: '05:00'`; `closeTimes: { mon…sun: '23:00' }`. Tuesday is locked at 23:00; the others can be set to 24:00 later (#27).
   118	- `weeklyCapHours: 20`, where the week runs from Mon 00:00 to the next Mon 00:00, America/Denver (C6).
   119	- `bookAheadDays: 14` (#49)
   120	- `startStepMinutes: 15`; `lengthChipsHours: [1,2,3,4,5,6]`; `maxLengthHours: 6`; `endTimeStepMinutes: 15` (#48)
   121	- `earlyCheckoutRefund: { stepMinutes: 15, rounding: 'up' }` (#48)
   122	- `timing: { checkInOpensBeforeMin: 15, reminderMin: 10, lastCallMin: 20, releaseMin: 30, stillHereBeforeEndMin: 10 }`
   123	- `extensionOptionsMin: [30, 60, 90, 120]`
   124	- `kilns: [{ name: 'Hestia' }, { name: 'Lumi' }]`
   125	- `links: { askClayHub: 'https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd-RhLmSXsrlzow3JK7m0H77pEp3Gg5_zo0eKxNBBru1v0QoA/viewform', membershipEmail: 'clayhub@tinkerartstudio.com' }`
     1	// My Clay Hub — a member's status from their Membership Manager record (DATA-MODEL.md, #34, #35, C8).
     2	//
     3	// Plain ES module: no Firebase, no clock. ingestMemberUpdate and the 3:30 AM recompute both call
     4	// deriveStatus; nothing else in My Clay Hub works out a member's status on its own.
     5	//
     6	// deriveStatus(source, todayDenver)
     7	//   source       null/undefined for a tombstone (no live record), else an object in the
     8	//                clayHub_members field shape: stage, scheduledPause {startDate, endDate},
     9	//                pauseHistory [{startDate, endDate} | {start, end}], scheduledCancellation
    10	//                {finalAccessDate}, plus tombstone/retired. Only these fields are read. Whatever the
    11	//                members/* projection stores, anything calling this (ingestMemberUpdate, the 3:30 AM
    12	//                recompute) must hand it this shape; a flattened shape would silently read as "no
    13	//                pause, no last day". Phase E tests that round trip.
    14	//   todayDenver  today's Denver calendar day, 'YYYY-MM-DD', passed in (see denverYMD in
    15	//                denver-time.js). Never read from the clock here.
    16	// Returns one of STATUSES. It never throws for any shape of source; it throws a TypeError only when
    17	// todayDenver itself isn't a valid date, because that is a caller bug, not member data.
    18	
    19	import { compareYMD, isValidYMD } from './denver-time.js';
    20	
    21	export const STATUSES = Object.freeze(['active', 'paused', 'review', 'offboarded', 'not_yet', 'removed']);
    22	
    23	export const STAGES = Object.freeze(['onboarding', 'touring', 'active', 'paused', 'offboarding', 'cancelled']);
    24	
    25	const isObject = value => typeof value === 'object' && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);
    26	const isAbsent = value => value === undefined || value === null;
    27	
    28	// A pause entry's start/end, in either spelling: startDate/endDate, or the legacy start/end.
    29	// The modern spelling wins when both are there.
    30	function pauseDates(entry) {
    31	  return {
    32	    start: isAbsent(entry.startDate) ? entry.start : entry.startDate,
    33	    end: isAbsent(entry.endDate) ? entry.end : entry.endDate,
    34	  };
    35	}
    36	
    37	// Every pause window from scheduledPause and each pauseHistory entry, as
    38	// { windows: [{ start, end }] (all valid), malformed: boolean }.
    39	// Malformed (rule 7, C8): a window that isn't an object, has a missing or invalid date, or ends before
    40	// it starts; or a pauseHistory that is present but isn't a list. A one-day pause (start = end) is valid.
    41	// No source (a tombstone) has no windows; a source that isn't a record is malformed.
    42	export function pauseWindows(source) {
    43	  if (isAbsent(source)) return { windows: [], malformed: false };
    44	  if (!isObject(source)) return { windows: [], malformed: true };
    45	  const entries = [];
    46	  let malformed = false;
    47	  if (!isAbsent(source.scheduledPause)) entries.push(source.scheduledPause);
    48	  if (!isAbsent(source.pauseHistory)) {
    49	    if (Array.isArray(source.pauseHistory)) entries.push(...source.pauseHistory);
    50	    else malformed = true;
    51	  }
    52	  const windows = [];
    53	  for (const entry of entries) {
    54	    if (!isObject(entry)) { malformed = true; continue; }
    55	    const { start, end } = pauseDates(entry);
    56	    if (!isValidYMD(start) || !isValidYMD(end) || compareYMD(end, start) < 0) { malformed = true; continue; }
    57	    windows.push({ start, end });
    58	  }
    59	  return { windows, malformed };
    60	}
    61	
    62	// The last day with access: { state: 'absent' | 'malformed' | 'valid', date? }.
    63	// Absent: no scheduledCancellation, or one with no finalAccessDate (null/undefined). Anything else
    64	// that isn't a valid 'YYYY-MM-DD', an empty string included, is malformed.
    65	function lastDay(source) {
    66	  const cancellation = source.scheduledCancellation;
    67	  if (isAbsent(cancellation)) return { state: 'absent' };
    68	  if (!isObject(cancellation)) return { state: 'malformed' };
    69	  const date = cancellation.finalAccessDate;
    70	  if (isAbsent(date)) return { state: 'absent' };
    71	  return isValidYMD(date) ? { state: 'valid', date } : { state: 'malformed' };
    72	}
    73	
    74	export function deriveStatus(source, todayDenver) {
    75	  if (!isValidYMD(todayDenver)) {
    76	    throw new TypeError(`todayDenver must be a valid 'YYYY-MM-DD' string, got ${JSON.stringify(todayDenver)}`);
    77	  }
    78	
    79	  // 1. No live source record (tombstone).
    80	  if (isAbsent(source) || (isObject(source) && (source.tombstone === true || source.retired === true))) return 'removed';
    81	  if (!isObject(source)) return 'review';
    82	
    83	  const stage = source.stage;
    84	  // 2. Not a member yet.
    85	  if (stage === 'onboarding' || stage === 'touring') return 'not_yet';
    86	  // 3. Missing or unknown stage.
    87	  if (!STAGES.includes(stage)) return 'review';
    88	
    89	  // 4. The last day: malformed → review; today after it → offboarded. The last day itself has access.
    90	  const last = lastDay(source);
    91	  if (last.state === 'malformed') return 'review';
    92	  if (last.state === 'valid' && compareYMD(todayDenver, last.date) > 0) return 'offboarded';
    93	
    94	  // 5. and 6. Cancelled or offboarding with no last day.
    95	  if (stage === 'cancelled' && last.state === 'absent') return 'offboarded';
    96	  if (stage === 'offboarding' && last.state === 'absent') return 'review';
    97	
    98	  // 7. Any malformed pause window (missing, invalid or reversed dates).
    99	  const pauses = pauseWindows(source);
   100	  if (pauses.malformed) return 'review';
   101	
   102	  // 8. Inside a pause window, both ends included.
   103	  if (pauses.windows.some(w => compareYMD(w.start, todayDenver) <= 0 && compareYMD(todayDenver, w.end) <= 0)) {
   104	    return 'paused';
   105	  }
   106	
   107	  // 9. Paused stage with no pause windows at all.
   108	  if (stage === 'paused' && pauses.windows.length === 0) return 'review';
   109	
   110	  // 10. Everything else.
   111	  return 'active';
   112	}
     1	rules_version = '2';
