/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n "members/|memberProfiles|staffRoster|phoneLast4|deriveStatus|reconcile|3:30|Membership Manager|one-way|sourceReadTime|tombstone" docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md' in /Users/christiehubley/my-clay-hub
 succeeded in 0ms:
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:20:| 10 | **No messaging.** "Notify everyone going" is a one-way notice | Two-way messaging is a big build and the place bugs pile up. Ask Clay Hub covers questions. | An in-app chat or inbox for replies. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:33:| 23 | **SUPERSEDED Sep 27 by #53.** ~~Membership Manager is the single source of truth, read directly, with no synced copy.~~ Membership Manager is **still** the single source of truth, and status still drives access automatically. But member data now reaches My Clay Hub through a **one-way projection** into its own project, because My Clay Hub lives in a separate Firebase project (#30). | Staff never update two systems (unchanged). | Syncing a separate copy of member data (now chosen, one-way only, because of #30). |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:34:| 24 | Full phone numbers never reach the members app or kiosk; the kiosk matches on the last 4 digits server-side. **Still stands.** Under #53 the projection carries `phoneLast4` only, worked out inside `tinker-hq-apps`. | Privacy. | Storing phones in the app. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:49:| 32 | D2 | Sep 27 | Server code in two codebases, `clayhub-link` (in studio-hub, the link only) and `my-clay-hub/functions`. Both deploy only through a functions-aware guard. | The link has to run where Membership Manager's data lives. Everything else stays in this app's own project. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:51:| 34 | D4 | Sep 27 | **A member's status is worked out by `deriveStatus`** from the dates, with Membership Manager's `stage` as a backstop. The rules are in a fixed order (DATA-MODEL.md), and the result is one of: active, paused, review, offboarded, not_yet, removed. Specific gaps give `review` (booking locked, feed still visible, staff flagged) instead of a lockout: a missing or unknown stage, a malformed last day, a pause with a missing or malformed date, `offboarding` with no last day, or `paused` with no pause dates. Every rule is in DATA-MODEL.md. The last access day itself still has access. | `stage` is only brought up to date when someone opens Membership Manager. Dates are the truth. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:53:| 36 | D5 | Sep 27 | Add an accurate **`memberSince`** to Membership Manager. Christie fills in missing phones. Member-since shows on Profile and in the Reports member panel. | There's no reliable join date today. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:54:| 37 | D6 | Sep 27 | **Nothing ever writes back to Membership Manager.** | Membership Manager re-saves whole records and would erase anything else. Any change to this would be a new, reviewed decision. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:69:| 52 | D21 | Sep 27 | Every member gets a **permanent `memberId`** in Membership Manager, plus a "Change email" action that keeps it. The change is **one atomic batch**: the new doc (same `memberId`, live) and the old doc marked `retired: true`. It **refuses** if a live doc already exists for the new email. Doc IDs stay as they are. | Email-based IDs collide, and an email change used to leave a stale second record. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:70:| 53 | D22 | Sep 27 | **The one-way link, "re-read, then send a snapshot"** (supersedes #23's "no copy"). When a member record changes, the link re-reads that member's current truth and sends a complete snapshot, stamped with when it was read. The newest snapshot always wins. Only name, email, status dates, member-since and `phoneLast4` are copied. | Correct even when changes arrive late, twice or out of order, and through deletes and email changes. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:75:| 58 | C8 | Sep 28 | A pause whose end is before its start is **malformed**, so `deriveStatus` gives `review` (rule 7). | Otherwise it would fall through to `active` silently; `review` is how #34 handles every other data gap. |
docs/my-clay-hub/DECISIONS.md:76:| 59 | — | Sep 28 | A pause with a start date but **no end date** gives **`review`**, not "paused indefinitely" (rule 7 as written). The member can sign in and see the feed but can't book; staff see a flag and add the end date, and the pause's booking cancellation happens then. | Christie chose it over the alternatives. The D-5 implementation review found Membership Manager's Quick Log can save a pause with a blank end, so this is a reachable state, not a typo. |
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:18:- see studio news (firing photos, updates) in a one-way feed,
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:24:**Not** Membership Manager. Membership Manager stays the system of record for members. My Clay Hub gets a **one-way copy** of just the fields it needs through a live link (§3), and never writes back.
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:36:- After sign-in, the app checks the membership (#33). The member must match **exactly one** live Membership Manager record by verified email, with a status that allows sign-in: **active**, **paused** or **review** (see §3).
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:54:## 3. Membership Manager integration (one-way link, separate project)
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:56:My Clay Hub doesn't read Membership Manager's collection directly: it's in a different Firebase project. A small function next to Membership Manager watches for changes and **re-sends a snapshot** of each changed member into My Clay Hub, usually within a minute. A check every 6 hours repairs anything missed (#53). Nothing is ever written back (#37).
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:58:**Fields copied:** name (first name and last initial are worked out from it), email, Membership Manager's status (`stage`), pause dates, last day, member-since (#36), and the **last 4 digits** of the cell phone (#24). Full phone numbers never leave Membership Manager's project.
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:60:**Member status** is worked out by one tested function from the **dates**, with Membership Manager's `stage` as a backstop, because `stage` is only brought up to date when someone opens Membership Manager (#34). The full rule order is in `DATA-MODEL.md`.
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:66:| **Review** | The membership record has a gap or an inconsistency (for example a pause with no end date). Can sign in and see the feed. **Booking is locked** with "We're checking your membership details — you can still see the feed." Staff see a flag to fix the record in Membership Manager. |
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:68:| **Not yet / Removed** | Onboarding or touring members, and records no longer live in Membership Manager, can't sign in. |
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:70:Status changes made in Membership Manager take effect automatically. Staff never update two systems. When a member's email changes, Membership Manager keeps their permanent member ID, so their bookings and history carry over (#52).
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:247:- Name, email and "Member since [date]", all from Membership Manager. If member-since is blank in Membership Manager, the line is hidden.
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:359:- **Members never get an account in `tinker-hq-apps`.** My Clay Hub is its own Firebase project, with its own rules. The only connection is the one-way link, which can read Membership Manager's records and can do nothing in My Clay Hub except call one private function (#30, #42).
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:381:- member-status recompute: daily at 3:30 AM Denver (it avoids the DST gap)
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:382:- the link's reconcile: every 6 hours
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:399:- make Membership Manager's saves reliable, fix its dates, and add a permanent member ID;
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:402:- build the one-way link.
docs/my-clay-hub/SPEC.md:448:- Writing anything back to Membership Manager (#37).

