108:  <li><strong>Running already?</strong> List this database's operations (<code>listOperationsAsync</code> on <code>projects/my-clay-hub/databases/(default)</code>, paged, filtered client-side to exports whose prefix starts <code>gs://&lt;bucket&gt;/weekly/D-</code>; <strong>cap: 1,000 operations examined</strong>, and hitting it throws — never "none"). A listed operation's <code>metadata</code> is a raw <code>google.protobuf.Any</code> (Firestore 9.3.0 <code>firestore_admin_v1_proto_api.d.ts:10355</code>): it is decoded with the pinned protobuf <strong>only</strong> when its type URL is exactly <code>type.googleapis.com/google.firestore.admin.v1.ExportDocumentsMetadata</code>, and the numeric <code>operationState</code> is mapped to its name. An operation with another type URL is not an export and is skipped; export metadata that fails to decode, or has an unknown state, throws (never treated as "not ours"). One not done → wait on it. One done <code>SUCCESSFUL</code> but no complete folder → throw (inconsistent: needs a person). Ones done <code>FAILED</code>/<code>CANCELLED</code> (or with <code>error</code>) are history: logged, never resumed, and their prefixes never reused → go to step 3. (This is V-4's bootstrap path.)</li>
