438:  <li><strong>Oct 2, V-3 implementation review round 1:</strong> Codex "merge after fixes" (2 blocking, 1 should-fix, 1 nit); Claude "merge after fixes" (5 should-fix, 6 nits). All applied except where noted: <strong>every call to Google is now held to the run's budget</strong> (new <code>deadline.js</code>: each call gets only the time left, and the client is passed the same timeout), so a stuck call can't carry a run past Cloud Run's kill (both reviewers; the fakes now model hung and slow calls); no export is started with under 5 min of budget left; <code>vaultFresh</code>'s listings get 20 s in all, so it always answers before its 30 s timeout; an unknown export state is judged only for exports of the run's own date (Claude); a fresh suffix never repeats a folder or prefix already seen (Claude); a page cap on folder listings (Claude); tests for the reachable "finished between the two listings" branch, the bucket reader's defensive branches, and <code>vaultExport</code>'s real wiring with only clients.js faked (Claude). DATA-RESTORE.md: the pre-restore copy is a manual Console export to <code>manual/pre-restore-&lt;date&gt;</code>, verified by its metadata file, never a Force run (both); a permission refusal stops for Christie's approval instead of widening (Codex); a scratch database is created deny-all (Claude). DECISIONS #63: only Christie, by hand, can import (Codex). V-4 gains the check above (Claude). <strong>Not changed:</strong> <code>firebase-admin</code> stays a direct dependency: it is a required peer dependency of firebase-functions 7.4.0 (npm would install it regardless), and V1 names it (Claude nit 10).</li>
